course: dictionary
lesson: 13874
title: Kidnapper: a word for a serious crime
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A kidnapper is a person who takes someone away by force or by tricks and keeps them as a prisoner. Kidnappers often want money before they let the person go.
explain: «The kidnappers sent a note asking for a ransom.» The word ransom is a clue. It is the money the kidnappers demand. You can see that the note is about money, so ransom must mean money paid to free someone.
explain: Stories, films and news use the word kidnapper when a serious crime is happening. Safety lessons teach children what to do if a stranger tries to take them away: shout, run, and tell a trusted adult.
fact: A kidnapper takes someone away by force or tricks and keeps them as a prisoner.
fact: «Kidnapper» is a noun. Its plural is «kidnappers».
fact: Kidnappers often ask for a ransom, which is money paid to free the person.
fact: Kidnapping is a serious crime, so the word tells the reader that something dangerous is happening.
fact: Safety rule: if a stranger tries to take you away, shout, run, and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The kidnapper took the boy by trickery and kept him locked in a cabin.» What is a kidnapper? | A friendly guide on a school trip | *A person who takes someone away and keeps them as a prisoner | A person who looks after lost pets | A person who sells old books
exercise: «The kidnappers sent a note asking for a ransom.» What is a ransom? | A kind of map used by explorers | A gift given on a birthday | *Money demanded before a prisoner is set free | A type of school lunch
exercise: A stranger says, «Come with me, I have a surprise for you.» What should you do? | Hide your phone and say nothing | *Shout, run, and tell a trusted adult | Go with them to see the surprise | Wait quietly and hope they go away
test: Which word means a person who takes someone away and keeps them as a prisoner? | Guide | Rescuer | Neighbour | *Kidnapper
test: Why do kidnappers often ask for a ransom? | To go on holiday | To give a prize | To make a new friend | *To get money
exam: Which word in a news story tells the reader that a serious crime is involved? | Sunshine | *Kidnapper | Picnic | Garden
